    <item>
      <title>Data Center Firm Elice Flops on Debut &amp; Merz's Russia Warning</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-10-20/daybreak-europe-10-20-2026-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">654dc57a04e989e21f73b319</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:05:34 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from Brussels, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

On today's show, AI jitters returned after the Korean data center firm Elice flopped on its stock market debut. Shares fell as much as 35% after its IPO, which raised $151 million.

Bloomberg has learnt that the AI cloud computing firm Nscale is in talks to sell computing power to Anthropic, in a deal that could be worth about $45 billion.

And tougher security measures, including an 11pm curfew in some parts of Paris and other cities, appear to have quelled violent protests in France for now.

Today's guest: Ana Boata, Allianz Trade, Head of Economic Research. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
